# RC1 exact-source integration patch/spec: PlatformImage + RG35XXImageCache
# Upstream owner remains org.recompile.mobile.PlatformImage.
# Do NOT create a replacement PlatformImage or a second image cache.
# Task: RGJ-RC1-006

Target: src/org/recompile/mobile/PlatformImage.java (TASEmulators/freej2me-plus devel)
Helper: src/org/recompile/mobile/RG35XXImageCache.java

## Byte-array constructor integration

In PlatformImage(byte[] imageData, int imageOffset, int imageLength, boolean mutable):

1. Preserve upstream argument/decode behavior. Only immutable images (`mutable == false`) are cache eligible.
2. Compute `rgCacheKey = RG35XXImageCache.keyForBytes(imageData, imageOffset, imageLength)`.
3. Query `RG35XXImageCache.CachedImage rgCached = RG35XXImageCache.get(rgCacheKey)`.
4. On hit, create a fresh `BufferedImage(rgCached.width, rgCached.height, BufferedImage.TYPE_INT_ARGB)`, obtain its `DataBufferInt`, copy `rgCached.pixels` into it, set `isMutable = false`, and return. The cache backing array is never exposed/shared.
5. On miss, preserve existing ImageIO decode and type normalization exactly.
6. PNG indexed transparency/tRNS compatibility repair, when present in the consolidated RG35XX PlatformImage path, MUST execute before cache insertion.
7. Insert final normalized/repaired pixels with `RG35XXImageCache.put(rgCacheKey, canvas.getWidth(), canvas.getHeight(), dataBuffer)` only for immutable images.
8. Preserve `isMutable = mutable` on the normal path.

Exact integration shape:

@@ PlatformImage(byte[] imageData, int imageOffset, int imageLength, boolean mutable)
+ String rgCacheKey = null;
+ if(!mutable)
+ {
+     rgCacheKey = RG35XXImageCache.keyForBytes(imageData, imageOffset, imageLength);
+     RG35XXImageCache.CachedImage rgCached = RG35XXImageCache.get(rgCacheKey);
+     if(rgCached != null)
+     {
+         canvas = new BufferedImage(rgCached.width, rgCached.height, BufferedImage.TYPE_INT_ARGB);
+         dataBuffer = ((DataBufferInt)canvas.getRaster().getDataBuffer()).getData();
+         System.arraycopy(rgCached.pixels, 0, dataBuffer, 0, rgCached.pixels.length);
+         isMutable = false;
+         return;
+     }
+ }
  // existing ImageIO decode/type normalization remains authoritative
  ...
  // existing/final RG35XX PNG/tRNS compatibility repair, if applicable
+ if(!mutable && rgCacheKey != null)
+     RG35XXImageCache.put(rgCacheKey, canvas.getWidth(), canvas.getHeight(), dataBuffer);
  isMutable = mutable;

## Cache API contract

`RG35XXImageCache` now owns dimensions with each immutable decoded entry:
- `CachedImage get(String key)` returns width, height and a defensive pixel copy.
- `put(String key, int width, int height, int[] pixels)` validates `width*height == pixels.length`, copies pixels and enforces the bounded LRU.
- byte-cost arithmetic uses long before narrowing, avoiding integer overflow.
- byte-slice validation uses `offset > data.length - length`, avoiding `offset + length` overflow.

This is a MODIFY of the existing registered class. No new RG35XX image/cache package or class is introduced.

## Mutable/immutable invariants

- PlatformImage(int Width, int Height) and color-backed blank images remain mutable and are never cached.
- PlatformImage(Image source) remains a deep copy via System.arraycopy; no cache sharing.
- PlatformImage(com.nttdocomo.ui.Image source) remains a deep copy; DoJa semantics are preserved.
- DoJa byte-array calls with mutable=true bypass cache completely.
- getMIDPGraphics()/getDoJaGraphics() immutable checks remain unchanged.
- Resource-name/InputStream constructors remain uncached in RC1 because they do not yet have a defined stable byte-identity key.
- Cached hit always reconstructs a new TYPE_INT_ARGB backing image.

## PNG/tRNS rule

Cache storage is downstream of the final RG35XX PNG/tRNS repair. A cache hit therefore represents the already-corrected ARGB result. The cache must never store a pre-repair indexed PNG decode.

## Duplicate-prevention result

Authoritative owner pair remains:
- PlatformImage: upstream facade/decoder and MIDP/DoJa semantics.
- RG35XXImageCache: only RG35XX immutable decoded-image cache.

Do not add RG35XXImageDecoder, RG35XXPngCache, RG35XXCachedImage or another image-cache owner.
